{{also|pýre}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|en|grk-pro|ine-pro}}
{{lbor|en|la|pyra|t=pyre, funeral pile}}, from {{der|en|grc|πυρά}}, from {{m|grc|πῦρ||fire}}. {{dbt|en|fire}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpaɪɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pyre.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|pyre}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪə(ɹ)|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[funeral]] [[pile]]; a combustible heap on which [[corpse]]s are burned.
#* For nine long nights, through all the dusky air, The '''pyres''' thick flaming shot a dismal glare.—[[Homer]] Iliad, p. 31
# Any [[heap]] or [[pile]] of [[combustible]]s.

